[~accountid:712020:79bdda29-2f20-4318-9d05-92c9d0bd7b47] To sum up our discussion today about Hypefy agreement, the agreement lacks several important clauses which we usually have in our agreement with agencies/influencers:

* Intellectual Property - license to Bolt to share content created by influencers' (we don’t always need ownership to their content; do they charge extra if Bolt shares the content?);
* Requirements to the content, e.g. obligations to act towards Bolt in good faith, follow the law and respect third party rights;
* Liability issues if Bolt suffers losses due to an influencer's mistake;

As Hypefy is not a regular agency but platform, we would also like to review terms/agreement between Hypefy and influencers.

Best,

Indrek

