Weekly automated reports on {{Food Safety}} incidents + provider related incidents using crisis channel, tagging Merchant OPS/AMs. 

CS does not have access to view occurrences for providers, so for any food safety and provider related safety incidents, we ask CS to fill out the report as {{1st Occurrence}}. This can later be updated by OPS/AMs team.

Further actions are determined by the Event Category:

h3. *Process outline*

[mapped out provider-related events here|https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/15tgyo-9jorgemsa_dX_SqYMTII1C-caiBGr8PDo44UM/edit?gid=522199485#gid=522199485]

# For events such as {{Allergic Reaction}}, {{Food Poisoning}}, {{Expired Product}}, {{Hazardous Object In Food}}, {{Tampering with Order,}} {{Contaminated Food}}:

* CS takes the report from the client and completes the initial investigation to fill out the report.
* *To be confirmed with Merchant team, if CS will continue investigating the issue with the Provider, and actioning feedback.*
* Replace Action Required with “Forward Feedback to the Provider” or “No Further Action”
* Merchant Operations/Account Managers to start sending feedback to providers based on weekly reports in crisis channels.

# The following events are escalated to Crisis Channels (provider hate speech + provider discrimination + provider inappropriate behaviour + provider use of sexual talk should be routed there).

* {{Unnecessary Contact by the Provider}}
* {{Intoxicated User Ordered and/or Was Served Alcohol}}
* {{Minor Ordered and/or Was Served Age Restricted Product}}
* {{Alcohol Sold After Hours}}
* {{Provider Discriminatory Acts}}
* {{Provider Use of Hate Speech}}
* {{Provider Unlawfully Detained The Courier}}
* {{Provider Unlawfully Detained The Eater}}
* {{Provider Threatens Physical Harm}}
* {{Provider Physically Assaults or Attempts to Assault Eater}}
* {{Provider Physically Assaults or Attempts to Assault Courier}}
* {{Provider Commits Homicide}}
* {{Provider Inappropriate Behaviour}}
* {{Provider Use of Any Sexual Talk}}
* {{Provider Groping Or Attempted Groping Of Courier}}
* {{Provider Rape Or Attempted Rape Of Eater}}
* {{Provider Rape Or Attempted Rape Of Courier}}
* {{Provider Sexually Touching or Exposing Themselves}}
* {{Provider Did Not Ask Eater for Age Verification}}
* If the reported party is the courier, CS can conduct the investigation as usual for the following events:
** {{Intoxicated User Ordered and/or Was Served Alcohol}}
** {{Minor Ordered and/or Was Served Age Restricted Product}}
** {{Alcohol Sold After Hours}}
* If reported party is the provider, Merchant Operations/Account Managers should take over the investigation. *To be confirmed with Merchant team*
** CS to fill out client/courier IDs, ticket and report details in the safety reporting tool. 
** CS will not fill out the {{Investigative}} section. 
** We will specify in the {{Investigative}} section in the Assessment Tool for these provider related events that Merchant Operations/Account Managers teams must fill out the rest of the report and contact the provider.
** CS will submit report as “not finalised”.
** The open report is automatically escalated to the #country-delivery-crisis-escalation channel where the event occurred in.
** The local Merchant Operations/Account Manager team will be tagged in the post to conduct the investigation with the provider and fill out, and finalise the {{Investigative}} section of the report, in addition to populating the {{Description of Events & Steps Taken}} field if needed. 
** Replace Action Required with “Forward Feedback to the Provider” or “No Further Action”

