We have recently accepted signing Bolt Business agreements with an entity from a non Bolt market exceptionally if the following conditions are met:

* it’s a reputable company with a valid use case (the company doesn’t have a suitable entity to use for contracting in a preferred market);
* we'd rely on England (or an EEA market Bolt operates in) for governing law/jurisdiction;
* possible implications it might have for billing and payments cleared with Tax/Finance;
* personal data transfer compliance managed (consulted with Privacy as needed);
* we don’t market or refer otherwise in our comms with the company as if services were offered to or in the respective market.

Feel free to explore this route also for this customer.

